1. Used to + V1

When used to means a past habit:

He used to work hard. ✅
She used to play tennis. ✅

Meaning: She played tennis regularly in the past, but it is not necessarily true now.

2. Be used to + noun / V-ing

When be used to means accustomed to:

He is used to hard work. ✅
He is used to working hard. ✅

Here, to is a preposition, so it is followed by a noun or gerund (V-ing).

❌ He is used to work hard.
✅ He is used to working hard.


3. Get used to + noun / V-ing

When get used to means become accustomed to:

He got used to working hard. ✅
He got used to hard work. ✅

❌ He got used to work hard.
✅ He got used to working hard.



4. Be used to + V1 (infinitive of purpose) — camels example

Camels are used to carry loads.
= Camels are utilized/employed in order to carry loads. (this describes the camel's function/purpose — passive voice: "people use camels to carry loads")

This is different again from #2:

Sentence	Meaning
Camels are used to carry loads.	Camels' function/purpose is carrying loads (passive + infinitive of purpose)
Camels are used to carrying loads.	Camels are accustomed to carrying loads (they're used to it, comfortable with it)



